{
  "suite": "placement",
  "level": 2,
  "about": "Which placement survives an import and which may be thrown away. A consumer cannot tell by looking at the collection kind, so the producer declares it.",
  "requires": {
    "features": [
      "placement"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "placement/semantic-must-survive",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "import",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "kind": "matrix",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": true,
            "regions": [
              "urgent-important",
              "calm-later"
            ]
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1",
              "region": "urgent-important"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "when": {
        "importInto": "a tool with no matrix view"
      },
      "with": {
        "placement": false
      },
      "simulated": true,
      "expect": {
        "fidelity": "reduced",
        "reports": [
          "placement"
        ],
        "result": {
          "members": [
            {
              "region": "urgent-important"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "why": "The region is a judgment the user made about the task, stored as a position. A tool that draws no grid must still keep the value and report that it cannot display it. Dropping it destroys the only record of the assessment."
    },
    {
      "id": "placement/view-may-be-dropped",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "import",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1",
              "context": {
                "x": 340,
                "y": 120
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "when": {
        "importInto": "a tool with no canvas"
      },
      "with": {
        "placement": false
      },
      "expect": {
        "fidelity": "full"
      },
      "why": "Canvas coordinates are furniture — where the user dragged something on one particular day. Discarding them loses nothing, and an import that reports reduced fidelity here will train users to ignore the warning that matters."
    },
    {
      "id": "placement/semantic-requires-named-regions",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "validate",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "kind": "matrix",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": true
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1",
              "context": {
                "x": 340,
                "y": 120
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "valid": false,
        "errors": [
          {
            "code": "placement.coordinates-not-semantic"
          }
        ]
      },
      "why": "A coordinate is meaningless outside the grid that produced it — the same point means different things at different zoom levels and window sizes. 'urgent-important' opens correctly in a tool that renders a plain list."
    },
    {
      "id": "placement/kanban-column-is-semantic",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "import",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "kind": "kanban",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": true,
            "regions": [
              "backlog",
              "doing",
              "shipped"
            ]
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1",
              "region": "doing"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "when": {
        "importInto": "a flat list tool"
      },
      "with": {
        "placement": false
      },
      "simulated": true,
      "expect": {
        "fidelity": "reduced",
        "reports": [
          "placement"
        ],
        "result": {
          "members": [
            {
              "region": "doing"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "why": "A kanban column is usually status wearing a position. Flattening the board loses the status of every card on it, which is the entire content of a board."
    },
    {
      "id": "placement/kanban-column-may-be-view",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "import",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "kind": "kanban",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          },
          "membership": {
            "mode": "query",
            "materialized": false
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1",
              "region": "doing"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "with": {
        "placement": false
      },
      "expect": {
        "fidelity": "full"
      },
      "why": "When a board's columns are generated from a status field the objects already carry, the column is a rendering of data held elsewhere and carries nothing of its own. Same kind, opposite answer — which is exactly why the collection kind cannot be trusted to imply the semantics."
    },
    {
      "id": "placement/labelled-region-survives",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "roundtrip",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "kind": "matrix",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": true,
            "regions": [
              "do",
              {
                "name": "delegate-wait",
                "label": "Delegate & Wait",
                "hermes:color": "#5fa4b5"
              }
            ]
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1",
              "region": "delegate-wait"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "when": {
        "importInto": "a tool that models regions as a list of names",
        "reexport": true
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": {
          "placement": {
            "regions": [
              "do",
              {
                "name": "delegate-wait",
                "label": "Delegate & Wait",
                "hermes:color": "#5fa4b5"
              }
            ]
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1",
              "region": "delegate-wait"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "why": "A region is a string OR an object, and the obvious implementation casts the list to string[] and indexes straight into it. That holds until a region grows a label, and then indexOf finds nothing: every member on the board silently loses its placement, the producer's own keys on the region are dropped, and the consumer reports it as the producer's fault. Two independent implementations made this exact mistake, and neither caught it, because the library each tested against happened to contain no labelled regions."
    },
    {
      "id": "placement/region-label-is-not-an-identifier",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "validate",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "kind": "matrix",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": true,
            "regions": [
              {
                "name": "delegate-wait",
                "label": "Delegate & Wait"
              }
            ]
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1",
              "region": "Delegate & Wait"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "valid": false,
        "errors": [
          {
            "code": "placement.region-not-declared"
          }
        ]
      },
      "why": "A member matches on `name`, never on `label`. Matching the display text works right up until somebody fixes a typo in the wording, at which point every card in that region points at a region that no longer exists — which is the whole reason the two are separate fields."
    },
    {
      "id": "placement/position-is-opaque",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "order",
      "given": {
        "members": [
          {
            "object": "o_0",
            "position": "Zz"
          },
          {
            "object": "o_1",
            "position": "a0"
          },
          {
            "object": "o_2",
            "position": "a0V"
          },
          {
            "object": "o_3",
            "position": "a1"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": [
        "o_0",
        "o_1",
        "o_2",
        "o_3"
      ],
      "why": "Ordering tokens sort byte-wise, not numerically or by locale. Under a language-aware collation 'Zz' sorts after 'a0' and the top of every list is wrong. Do not parse these as numbers and do not re-generate them on import."
    }
  ]
}
